{
  "dom_id": "step-q89161",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following transformations map any polygon to a similar polygon?\n\nI. Stretching with stretch factor $6$ in the $x$-direction, then a translation by $2$ units downward\n\nII. Rotation by ${45}^{∘}$ clockwise around a point $O$ followed by reflection over a line $l$\n\nIII. Dilation of scale factor $4$ with center at $A,$ then translation by $6$ units to the right",
  "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations.\n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I includes stretching in only one direction. Thus, it is not a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II is a combination of rotation and a reflection, which are rigid motions. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III is a combination of dilation of scale factor $4$ and a translation. Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
